validator tests

test_date_gate_excludes_later_building:
  pass  1836 building excluded from an 1835 scene
  pass  date gate produces no error for a legitimate exclusion

test_overlapping_phases_are_an_error:
  pass  two phases covering one scene date is a hard error

test_epoch_must_cover_scene_date:
  pass  scene date outside its terrain epoch is an error
  pass  unresolvable terrain epoch is an error

test_review_required_blocks_release:
  pass  review_required blocks a scene from being released

test_a_flagged_household_blocks_release:
  pass  a flagged household blocks a scene from being released
  pass  a flagged PERSON blocks a scene from being released
  pass  an unflagged household does not block release

test_exclusions_cannot_contradict_the_dataset:
  pass  a structure both excluded and resolving into the scene is an error

test_an_exclusion_expires_at_its_own_earliest_scene:
  pass  an 1837 building is legitimately excluded from an 1835 scene
  pass  the same entry excluded from its own earliest scene is an error
  pass  a scene that does not list `exclusions` is not held to the 1835 town's record

test_exclusions_carry_a_reason_and_a_citation_that_resolves:
  pass  a named, reasoned, cited exclusion passes
  pass  a citation that resolves in no source record is an error
  pass  excluding a structure with no citation at all is an error
  pass  an exclusion with no stated reason is a deletion, and an error

test_the_watch_list_stops_a_promotion_it_only_used_to_ask_for:
  pass  an open question on an inferred claim passes
  pass  the same claim promoted to documented is an error
  pass  an entry in the dataset that does not name the claim carrying the doubt fails
  pass  carried_by naming a phase the record does not have is an error
  pass  carried_by naming something that is not a graded claim is an error
  pass  declaring in_dataset with no such record is an error
  pass  a committed record the entry still calls unbuilt is an error
  pass  a citation that resolves in no source record is an error
  pass  no sources and no stated reason for having none is an error
  pass  no sources WITH the reason stated passes
  pass  a dossier file that is not committed is an error
  pass  a dossier anchor that is not in the file is an error
  pass  an entry with no question at all is an error
  pass  an id that is both excluded and an open question is an error
  pass  carried_by naming a claim the provenance card renders no section for is an error
  pass  carried_by naming a block that carries no confidence of its own is an error
  pass  carried_by naming the footprint, which the card does render, passes
  pass  every claim the map pairs with a card section is one the card reads

test_confidence_contract:
  pass  documented without a source is an error
  pass  documented citing an unresolvable source is an error
  pass  derived without stated reasoning is an error
  pass  derived with reasoning passes
  pass  inferred citing the source that bounds it is fine
  pass  inferred without stated reasoning is still an error

test_wide_range_rule_targets_guesses_not_facts:
  pass  a documented 20-year span does not warn (the Sauganash stood that long)
  pass  an undocumented 40-year span warns
  pass  a reversed range is an error

test_presence_is_held_to_the_confidence_contract:
  pass  a documented span with no source is an error
  pass  a documented span citing a resolving source passes
  pass  an inferred span with reasoning and no source passes

test_the_card_is_fed_the_claims_it_renders:
  pass  the 1835 scene has sidecars to check
  pass  the card reads documented_range
  pass  every 1835 sidecar carries documented_range
  pass  the card reads change_note
  pass  every 1835 sidecar carries change_note
  pass  the card reads placement.position_note
  pass  every 1835 sidecar carries placement.position_note
  pass  the card reads placement.position_sources
  pass  every 1835 sidecar carries placement.position_sources
  pass  the card reads placement.position_confidence
  pass  every 1835 sidecar carries placement.position_confidence
  pass  every 1835 sidecar states a dated span and how sure it is

test_liberties_cover_inferred_inventions:
  pass  an inferred footprint with no liberty at all is an error
  pass  an inferred position with no liberty at all is an error
  pass  claiming the footprint and the placement satisfies the check
  pass  prose about footprints and placement does not cover them — only a claim does
  pass  the error says which liberties do name the building
  pass  the error shows the Covers token that would fix it
  pass  a phase-scoped claim does not silently cover a sibling phase
  pass  a structure-scoped claim covers every phase that drew that aspect
  pass  a claim against a structure that does not exist is an error
  pass  a claim against a phase that does not exist is an error
  pass  claiming an invention that the data no longer contains is an error
  pass  the same claim under Resolved is not an error — evidence is allowed to arrive
  pass  an empty liberties file is an error, not a silent pass

test_liberties_cover_invented_form:
  pass  an inferred form attribute with no claim is an error
  pass  owning up to the geometry does not cover what the record says the building was
  pass  the error shows the form token that would fix it
  pass  claiming the form attribute satisfies the check
  pass  a documented form attribute is never required to be claimed
  pass  claiming an attribute that is not inferred is an error

test_geometry_declaration_is_required_for_unread_attributes:
  pass  an attribute the archetype never reads must declare what the mesh does
  pass  an attribute the archetype does read needs no declaration
  pass  declaring geometry on an attribute the archetype builds is an error
  pass  admitting to omitting a value the record says is false is an error
  pass  a rejected reading declares record_only and passes
  pass  a geometry state outside the vocabulary is an error
  pass  an archetype with no declared CONSUMED set is skipped, not indicted

test_liberties_cover_omissions_and_simplifications:
  pass  an attested feature the mesh omits with no liberty is an error
  pass  a value a fixed default stands in for is an error too
  pass  the error says the model does not show what the record states
  pass  a rejected reading owes no admission
  pass  an attribute the archetype builds owes no admission
  pass  claiming both discharges them
  pass  claiming to have omitted something that is built is an error
  pass  with no CONSUMED map the omission rule reports nothing rather than guessing

test_liberties_cover_what_the_ground_invents:
  pass  an inferred bank face with no liberty at all is an error
  pass  an inferred swale with no liberty at all is an error
  pass  the error quotes the token that would discharge it
  pass  a documented ground claim owes no admission
  pass  claiming both ground inventions satisfies the check
  pass  a claim against another epoch does not discharge this one's invention
  pass  and the claim against an epoch that is not committed is itself an error
  pass  claiming to have invented a documented ground claim is an error
  pass  a resolved entry may keep a claim the evidence has settled
  pass  a claim on a block the spec does not grade is an error
  pass  a ground admission does not cover a building's invented outline
  pass  and the ground's own claims stay discharged while it fails
  pass  with no terrain index the ground rule reports nothing rather than guessing

test_the_checked_ground_is_the_ground_on_the_panel:
  pass  the index is built off the compiler the panel renders from
  pass  a zone added to the spec is owed an admission the day it appears
  pass  and the gate demands it by name

test_the_committed_ground_admits_to_everything_it_invents:
  pass  the committed terrain states inventions a visitor walks on
  pass  and docs/LIBERTIES.md admits to every one of them

test_archetypes_declare_what_they_consume:
  pass  every params module declares a CONSUMED set
  pass  the shipped archetypes are covered
  pass  the sets name real parameters, not prose

test_consumed_attributes_actually_reach_the_parameters:
  pass  every consumed attribute the records state changes the parameters
  pass  the check had real attributes to exercise
  pass  an attribute the resolver ignores does not move the parameters
  pass  an attribute the resolver reads does

test_covers_field_parses_to_claims:
  pass  a two-segment token covers the structure, not one phase
  pass  a three-segment token names its phase
  pass  well-formed tokens report no problems
  pass  a form token keeps its prefix as part of the aspect
  pass  a form token without a phase covers the structure
  pass  well-formed form tokens report no problems
  pass  a terrain token parses into the terrain domain, not into a structure
  pass  a ground claim keeps the group its id carries
  pass  well-formed terrain tokens report no problems
  pass  both domains round-trip to the text the document wrote
  pass  a terrain token without an epoch is reported, not read as a structure
  pass  a terrain token naming no claim is reported
  pass  an aspect outside the vocabulary is reported
  pass  a bare structure id is reported
  pass  prose in a Covers field is reported, not silently parsed
  pass  a Covers field that claims nothing is reported

test_mesh_input_hash_tracks_geometry_not_prose:
  pass  rewriting a note does not make a mesh stale
  pass  a geometry declaration does not make a mesh stale
  pass  adding a source citation does not make a mesh stale
  pass  the phase's own prose does not make a mesh stale
  pass  a value the archetype reads makes the mesh stale
  pass  a confidence change makes the mesh stale, because it is shaded into the geometry
  pass  a redrawn footprint makes the mesh stale
  pass  renaming an attribute to the name the archetype reads is a rebuild
  pass  the derived properties are inside the hash

test_manifest_declares_the_scheme_the_generators_compute:
  pass  the committed manifest was stamped under the current scheme

test_ground_contact_measures_the_whole_outline:
  pass  a building on flat ground lands
  pass  a building whose far corner hangs over a drop does not land

test_ground_contact_tolerance_is_the_step_up_rule:
  pass  a step a person could take is not a finding
  pass  a step a person could not take is

test_ground_contact_of_a_crossing_is_its_deck:
  pass  a deck 2.22 m over banks 1.0 m high does not land
  pass  the same deck at bank height lands, and the water between is not counted

test_ground_contact_declaration_is_checked_both_ways:
  pass  a structure standing off the ground and saying nothing is an error
  pass  declaring it satisfies the check
  pass  declaring it while sitting on the ground is an error too
  pass  a state with no reasoning is an error

test_ground_contact_owes_the_liberties_document_an_entry:
  pass  a structure that reaches no ground and no liberty saying so is an error
  pass  claiming it satisfies the check
  pass  claiming a landing that is fine is an over-claim

test_sidecar_shape_includes_only_indexed_structure_versions:
  pass  a version-only emitted field joins the structure-sidecar contract
